WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.621
One method for every claim.

2
00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:09.411
This elective has examined claims about scaling, benchmarks, model quality, timelines, critics, work, safety, and law.

3
00:00:09.691 --> 00:00:13.787
They differ in subject, but you have been applying the same method each time.

4
00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:22.813
This lesson makes it explicit, gives you two quantitative tools to support it, works one example end to end, and then steps back to the whole program.

5
00:00:23.093 --> 00:00:26.080
The method has six parts: Who says it, with what access?

6
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:32.803
A lab leader sees unreleased models; an academic sees published data; a journalist sees the speaker.

7
00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:35.963
Access is a reason to listen, not to believe.

8
00:00:36.243 --> 00:00:37.544
What are their incentives?

9
00:00:37.824 --> 00:00:44.352
Fundraising, product launches, regulatory positioning, contrarian visibility, a competing approach.

10
00:00:44.632 --> 00:00:50.285
Incentives do not make a claim false; they set how much independent evidence you should require.

11
00:00:50.565 --> 00:00:51.803
What kind of evidence?

12
00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:58.973
Randomized experiment, field study, benchmark, usage data, vendor-run eval, expert opinion, anecdote.

13
00:00:59.253 --> 00:01:01.941
Each answers a different question (lesson 6).

14
00:01:02.221 --> 00:01:03.885
Measured or extrapolated?

15
00:01:04.165 --> 00:01:10.203
Which part was observed, on what population, and which part extends a trend beyond it (lesson 1)?

16
00:01:10.483 --> 00:01:11.741
What are the base rates?

17
00:01:12.021 --> 00:01:14.645
How often have claims of this kind held up before?

18
00:01:14.925 --> 00:01:17.848
Has it been replicated, or can you test it yourself?

19
00:01:18.128 --> 00:01:22.672
Independent replication, or a small eval on your own task (lesson 3).

20
00:01:22.952 --> 00:01:28.797
Then write a verdict: one paragraph, ending with a confidence level and the evidence that would change it.
